<title>USA: U.S. Q3 current account gap widened to $47.96 bln.</title>
<headline>U.S. Q3 current account gap widened to $47.96 bln.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. current account,</p>
<p>seasonally adjusted, as reported by the Commerce Department.</p>
<p>In Billions of Dlrs/Credits:</p>
<p>    -		  Q3 1996    Q2'96--Rev from    Q1'96</p>
<p> Current Account    -47.96   -40.21   -38.78    -34.87</p>
<p> Goods Balance	-51.59   -47.00   -46.83    -42.73</p>
<p> Services Balance    17.76    18.42    18.96     18.50</p>
<p> Invest.Income Bal.  -4.71    -2.26    -1.60	0.26</p>
<p> Total Exports	253.84   257.01   257.52    252.65</p>
<p> Goods Exports	149.94   153.10   153.32    150.03</p>
<p> Services Exports    55.60    55.90    56.01     55.12</p>
<p>In Billions of Dlrs/Credits:</p>
<p>    -		  Q3 1996    Q2'96--Rev from    Q1'96</p>
<p> Total Imports     -292.38  -287.85  -287.00   -276.61</p>
<p> Goods Imports     -201.53  -200.09  -200.15   -192.76</p>
<p> Services Imports   -37.84   -37.48   -37.05    -36.62</p>
<p> Govt. Transfers     -9.42    -9.37    -9.30    -10.90</p>
<p> U.S.Assets Abroad  -54.68   -50.73   -49.17    -68.75</p>
<p> Foreign-HeldAssets 124.00   100.55    80.32     99.47</p>
<p>Net data--Govt. transfers, U.S. assets abroad and foreign-held assets.  </p>
<p>The department said net recorded capital inflows were $69.3 billion in the third quarter, compared with $49.8 billion in the second quarter.</p>
<p>The department said acquisitions of U.S. assets by foreigners accelerated more than purchases of foreign assets by U.S. residents.</p>
<p>The third quarter deficit on current account was a record surpassing the previous record shortfall of $43.2 billion set nearly nine years ago in the fourth quarter of 1987.  </p>
<p>The increase in the third quarter current account deficit was accounted for by bigger deficits on both goods and services and on investment income, the department said.</p>
